> API and interpretation

ZDT1 uses f1=x1 and f2=g(1-sqrt(f1/g)), with g=1+9*mean(x2..xn). The analytic
front requires the other coordinates zero; observed signed vertical gaps
summarize approximation only. Objectives must be finite and have consistent
positive dimension. Bounds have finite strict spans, and rates/eta controls are
checked. Zero generations retain historical initial callback evaluations but
return an empty archive front. Fitness dominance counters exclude the separately
filtered final front; all counters state their scope.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Zitzler, Laumanns and Thiele (2001), SPEA2, TIK Report103|https://doi.org/10.3929/ethz-a-004284029]

